\title{The Sumcheck Protocol}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    One protocol, used everywhere: GKR, [Spartan](dhsorens-003G), [HyperPlonk](dhsorens-003H),
    Basefold, logUp-GKR, [WHIR](dhsorens-003C). It is the first thing [ArkLib](dhsorens-0040)
    formalised, and probably the right place to start reading Lean.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The protocol and [its soundness error](dhsorens-004L), stated with the degree and
        variable count explicit.}
        \li{Prover cost: the linear-time algorithm, and what changes when the base field is small.}
        \li{Batching several sumchecks; zero-knowledge variants.}
        \li{Reducing a claim about a polynomial to an evaluation — the interface by which sumcheck
        meets a [commitment scheme](dhsorens-002Z).}
        \li{Why the [Fiat–Shamir attack](dhsorens-002G) landed on GKR, a sumcheck-based protocol,
        and what that implies about parameterisation.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [ArkLib](https://github.com/Verified-zkEVM/ArkLib) (\code{ProofSystem/Sumcheck}).
}
